<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <description>Grants SF Bulk Loader E2E access to the SfblE2E external client app (JWT bearer flow)</description>
    <label>Sfbl E2E</label>
    <!--
      SFBL-327 TODO: After metadata deploy and permset assignment, create a SetupEntityAccess record
      linking this permission set to the SfblE2E ECA. Without this record, AdminApprovedPreAuthorized
      does not activate and JWT bearer auth fails.

      The SetupEntityAccess link is a runtime data record (not metadata) and cannot be deployed
      via sf project deploy start. SFBL-325 setup_scratch_org.sh must execute the equivalent of:

        Query PermissionSet where Name=SfblE2EPermSet to get ParentId.
        Query ExternalClientApplication where DeveloperName=SfblE2E to get SetupEntityId.
        sf data create record, sobject SetupEntityAccess,
          values ParentId, SetupEntityId, SetupEntityType=ExternalClientApplication.

      See SPIKE_REPORT.md and tests/e2e/sf/scripts/setup_scratch_org.sh for the proven flow.
    -->
</PermissionSet>
